  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 239 AM MDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nUpper level trof which brought the showers and isolated\nthunderstorms yesterday continues to push rapidly east. Will\nhave much drier and warmer conditions today with skies becoming\nsunny after some patchy fog this morning. Will see the warmest\ntemperatures of the week Thursday and Friday with many low\nelevation locations near 80 degrees. A cold front will move\nthrough eastern Idaho Friday and expect breezy to windy\nconditions with highs again near 80 in lower elevations. Behind\nthe cold front it will be much cooler over the weekend with\nhighs Saturday in the 50s mountains and 60s valleys. There will\nonly be a slight chance for showers and thunderstorms Sunday and\nMonday but not expecting any significant amounts.",
